{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil","id":637473,"title":"Question regarding Working together and good vs evil","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-23T15:48:04-07:00","id":637473,"title":"Question regarding Working together and good vs evil","content":"I had an disagreement with some friends. Some of my friends are convinced that the vast majority of werewolves are all holy paladins working for the greater good and that vampires are also good guys and the camorilia I think it was works to make sure that humans don't die and protects them.<br /> <br /> I think all of that is bullshit because well....they are vampires and mother fuckign werewolves...humans are their food and if humans knew they existed they outnumber and out gun them 10 to 1.<br /> <br /> Where in the vampire and werewolf books do I need to find the parts that I can disillusion their views on these things? I haven't read those two books all the way through and only read the character creation stuff really. So a lot of the fluff in those two books is unknown to me. So where do I find it at:?<br /> <br /> Also, where do I find any info on interactions between the two groups? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7409,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7409-veil","user":"veil","date":". 08-23-2015, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7409-veil","name":"veil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T16:36:40-07:00","id":637518,"title":"","content":"Tell them to read the core book just once. Really this is all over the place.<br /> <br /> Werwolves are pretty much all holy paladins, they got that right. In the sense that they are all fanatics who fight against the Wyrm. They don't give a shit about humans, except for personal reasons. They have a rule that says &quot;dont eat them&quot;, but nothing about not killing humans. Hell they purged humanity for centuries some millenia ago. They fight against the force that wants to bring the world around them down. A force that often uses humans as pawns. On the other side most of them began their life as a human. But felt estranged all their life. Think of them as mildly sociopathic soldiers fighting for the greater good. Humans are colletral damage for the more dutybound and playthings for thos less morally inclined.<br /> <br /> Vampires are all egoistic jackasses. The cam does not protect mortals. They are perfectly fine with you killing humans as long as you hide the corpses. If you don't they will come and clean up the mess - probably by killing MORE humans (pesky witnesses) and then whoever causes the mess.<br /> <br /> As for interactions between the two. Werewolves think Vampires stink of the Wyrm for most parts. So the average interaction is the werewolf tearing a vampire apart. Vamps are scared shitless of lupines and mostly try to never stray out into the wild because of them (and the lack of tasty food).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T19:19:33-07:00","id":637633,"title":"","content":"If I were going to compare vampires and werewolves to humans, I wouldn't say paladins. Werewolves are kinda like ISIS and so are the Sabbat. The Camarilla is more like a drug cartel - a little easier to work with than ISIS but no less evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T21:45:46-07:00","id":637721,"title":"","content":"It can occasionally be a bit of a misnomer to go with &quot;fanatical religious&quot; for Garou and Fera. Quite a lot of Changers can be very irreligious. However, when they talk about spirits that they can see but others generally can't, the outside observation places them there, even when those beings are quite real and the protocols for dealing with them are just the restrictions of the spirits' natures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=637518#post637518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for interactions between the two. Werewolves think Vampires stink of the Wyrm for most parts. So the average interaction is the werewolf tearing a vampire apart. Vamps are scared shitless of lupines and mostly try to never stray out into the wild because of them (and the lack of tasty food).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just in their heads. Anyone dropping below Humanity 7 is embracing corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T23:57:44-07:00","id":637744,"title":"","content":"Saying that any Humanity below 7 equals embracing corruption is way too simple.<br /> <br /> But, either way, those folks read so little about the setting that is even cute!<br /> <br /> Really, the only safe definition in the WoD is &quot;shades of grey&quot;. If you assume any group as good or evil by default, you're probably wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T01:19:48-07:00","id":637767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=637744#post637744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying that any Humanity below 7 equals embracing corruption is way too simple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not for a Garou. But be sure to remind the frothing monster that it is being a judgmental bigot, and that it isn't your fault; you just had a bad night and drained that poor gangbanger of his last few drops of lifeblood <i>on accident...</i><br /> <br /> And Saur makes a very interesting point on non-religious Garou. What is the purpose of faith when you can stride into the umbra and have a conversation with an aspect of one of the gods? The existence of such things stops being a matter of <i>faith</i>; it's a matter of <i>fact</i>. Many Garou know (or suspect) that the most powerful beings in all of creation are either insane or insensate. In such a setting I think you can still have faith, but it is by no means a requirement to want to bring about an end to the Wyrm's machinations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 08-24-2015, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T03:54:07-07:00","id":637837,"title":"","content":"Even for a Garou, first because most Garou don't have any notion of Humanity (the trait) and its relation with the &quot;scent&quot; of Wyrm in the vampire. Also, a lot of corrupted things aren't &quot;embracing&quot; said corruption. And none of those maters to the average Garou.<br /> <br /> To them it is like this: every vampire is corrupted, everything that is corrupted stinks of Wyrm if you can sense it, and the Wyrm have to be dealt with. &quot;Embrace&quot; corruption carries a notion of acknowledging it and choosing to live with it. From the vampire's side it is an oversimplification, from the Werewolf side it is irrelevant. The presence of said corruption is the real mater.<br /> <br /> By the way, most <u>mortals</u> have less than Humanity 7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T04:24:17-07:00","id":637878,"title":"","content":"Most mortals are feeding the Wyrm. It's just that Vampires are direct servants of Eater of Souls unless they really keep a tight reign on their behaviours. The act of their existence and feeding is what makes them problematic, even if they try balancing it out with good and kindly deeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T09:52:59-07:00","id":638120,"title":"","content":"I'd recommend that they read anything with Red Talons in it, if they insist on seeing Werewolves as &quot;good guys&quot; (or at least pro-human good guys.) For that matter, a lot of the changing breeds have a different idea about the Garou than your friends do.<br /> <br /> It's harder to specifically disillusion someone about the Camarilla, I suspect, because they have remarkably good press. They do maintain the masquerade after all, though that's less about saving humans than about protecting themselves. I think maybe the best thing to do there is to recommend that they read more of the splat fiction. Seeing Jan Pieterzoon make sure he can feed would perhaps be a good reminder that even the &quot;nicer&quot; vampires are pretty much bastards.<br /> <br /> Most of the core books will address generally how the two groups interact. Short answer: not well. But other folk here have already elaborated on that. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 08-24-2015, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T20:49:50-07:00","id":638769,"title":"","content":"They don't need to read the splat fiction. Just finish reading the actual core books. You guys are losing very good books and the answers you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T15:50:46-07:00","id":639537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>veil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil#post637473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an disagreement with some friends. Some of my friends are convinced that the vast majority of werewolves are all holy paladins working for the greater good and that vampires are also good guys and the camorilia I think it was works to make sure that humans don't die and protects them.<br /> <br /> I think all of that is bullshit because well....they are vampires and mother fuckign werewolves...humans are their food and if humans knew they existed they outnumber and out gun them 10 to 1.<br /> <br /> Where in the vampire and werewolf books do I need to find the parts that I can disillusion their views on these things? I haven't read those two books all the way through and only read the character creation stuff really. So a lot of the fluff in those two books is unknown to me. So where do I find it at:?<br /> <br /> Also, where do I find any info on interactions between the two groups?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire the Masquerade, Revised Core Book. The section regarding sect and Clans with stereotypes and all.<br /> Werewolf the Apocalypse, Revised Core Book. The section regarding Tribes, Auspices and the whole Metis treatment.<br /> <br /> <br /> by the way, interaction Werewolves &amp; Vampires usually are a bloody thing (on the Appendix of both books there's a paragraph regarding the view of the other group).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T10:28:26-07:00","id":641795,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't call the Garou or Kindred as a whole good. I mean most of the worlds problems exist because of them, such as The War of Rage. They kinda drove the Were-Bats to extinction, who were there allies until they started committing genocide. If the Cammies protect humans, its only in the same way we protect Cows. Their are exceptions, though that's mainly player characters.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T12:46:26-07:00","id":641956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=641795#post641795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't call the Garou or Kindred as a whole good. I mean most of the worlds problems exist because of them, such as The War of Rage. They kinda drove the Were-Bats to extinction, who were there allies until they started committing genocide.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No one else knows it, but the Nagah labor under the burden of the truth that one of their own fired the first shots into the powderkeg that became the War of Rage for power granted from the Wyrm. The Garou are still to blame, but the serpents blame themselves far, far more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T14:22:01-07:00","id":642090,"title":"","content":"I think the Camarilla does try to make sure humans don't die <i>out. </i>On an individual basis, yeah, they don't give a shit, but if something threatened the entire <i>species</i> I think they'd have our collective back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T15:28:24-07:00","id":642146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=642090#post642090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Camarilla does try to make sure humans don't die <i>out. </i>On an individual basis, yeah, they don't give a shit, but if something threatened the entire <i>species</i> I think they'd have our collective back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they'd lord it over the survivors like the aliens that kept Star Lord around in his youth did to him. &quot;I stopped them from eating you! Be grateful and let me drain a few pints!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T16:15:39-07:00","id":642179,"title":"","content":"Also I can't get over how &quot;holy paladins working for the greater good&quot; manages to be literally true on such a humongously technical level. It's like, they <i>are</i> but in a way that's completely divorced from what those words usually mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T16:57:09-07:00","id":642194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=642179#post642179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I can't get over how &quot;holy paladins working for the greater good&quot; manages to be literally true on such a humongously technical level. It's like, they <i>are</i> but in a way that's completely divorced from what those words usually mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shrug. Their god is Gaia and the Garou Nation is on a worldwide crusade. Calling them paladins is just a nicer way of saying 'bloody minded religious fanatic.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T17:41:46-07:00","id":642234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=637633#post637633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were going to compare vampires and werewolves to humans, I wouldn't say paladins. Werewolves are kinda like ISIS and so are the Sabbat. The Camarilla is more like a drug cartel - a little easier to work with than ISIS but no less evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much spot on. <br /> <br /> Werewolves are zealous crusaders out to do what they believe is correct, and if they have to murder people on the way, they're more than willing to do so. A good look at any violently religious &quot;end of the world&quot; sect is a great place to get a feel for where werewolves and the Sabbat are coming from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T00:51:50-07:00","id":643862,"title":"","content":"Does a good act become wicked because it was done for wicked intentions? Does a wicked act become good because it was done for righteous intentions? These are questions that have confounded people for centuries. Lets use an example of a Camarilla vampire. Jan Peterzoon, he's a ventrue. His Feeding restriction is Rape victims. Inorder to have easy and regular access to his food he funds and supports Women's shelters throughout the world. One can look at his act as farming these women, yet even they benefited when they had no place to go, and that ignores all the countless ones he never touches. If it weren't for his selfishness these shelters would not exist, these women would have no place to go.<br /> <br /> Jan is the camarilla in microcosm. It tries to make the world better for mortals in a purely selfish reasons. It improves neighborhoods because the Sabbat and to a lesser extent the Anarchs find feeding easier and more plentiful in shitholes. It spreads human habitat in order to make feeding easy. It fights demons and monsters because they are a threat to Camarilla power. Nothing they do is altruistic on a large scale(though vampires are like people individuals), but they can and do do things that people might call good.<br /> <br /> The Garou nation believes it works to defend the World or possibly all life in the universe. They are all so petty, vindictive, xenophobes who can't even work well with other people who change into animals because they had to dominate them. The Garou are very good at justifying their actions in righteous language claiming betrayals by other Fera, or that being corrupted is enough reason to die(vs being clensed). A sizeable minority feel that all humans should be wiped out and probably the majority while not willing to be part of a culling to more &quot;managable levels&quot; wouldn't shed any tears if that happened through more natural means. Most wouldn't cry tears if our civilzation colapsed most starved to death(&quot;Its natural!&quot;) and humanity was forced into a more simple existence..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T02:00:33-07:00","id":643889,"title":"","content":"The horrible thing is... the Garou are right. Not about being unable to play well with others like them, but everything else. The world in Werewolf is a horrifying cesspit, and it's only getting worse day by day. Honestly, it's the worst WoD of them all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T04:01:08-07:00","id":643921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=643889#post643889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The horrible thing is... the Garou are right. Not about being unable to play well with others like them, but everything else. The world in Werewolf is a horrifying cesspit, and it's only getting worse day by day. Honestly, it's the worst WoD of them all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are they? Garou claim humanity isn't special. But whole ecosystems in the Umbra exist built on human action and thought. This isn't something Beaver Dams do. This isn't something Termite Mounds do. Its something humans and humans alone do. There are wolf spirits. There are Deer spirits. There are no human spirits. There's 2 whole layers completely dedicated to human endevors that Garou have a hard time entering.<br /> <br /> Is the power of the Wyrm apparent? Yes. Does that mean that being a 9 foot tall murder machine is the best solution to the problem at hand? Well I think that's the tragedy of W:TA they are a hammer given the sacred job of hammer nails unfortunately their problems are all nuts and bolts and screws if they are lucky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T07:33:37-07:00","id":644110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=643921#post643921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are they? Garou claim humanity isn't special. But whole ecosystems in the Umbra exist built on human action and thought. This isn't something Beaver Dams do. This isn't something Termite Mounds do. Its something humans and humans alone do. There are wolf spirits. There are Deer spirits. There are no human spirits. There's 2 whole layers completely dedicated to human endevors that Garou have a hard time entering.<br /> <br /> Is the power of the Wyrm apparent? Yes. Does that mean that being a 9 foot tall murder machine is the best solution to the problem at hand? Well I think that's the tragedy of W:TA they are a hammer given the sacred job of hammer nails unfortunately their problems are all nuts and bolts and screws if they are lucky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before the Deep Umbra got changed into a stretch of the High Umbra in W20, there was, at most, one level, and it was because there was such a monumental quantity of self-loathing and fear of death in humans. If you want to call their disconnection and estrangement from the world around them special, that's great, but Werewolf doesn't tend to look on it favorably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T08:04:13-07:00","id":644161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=644110#post644110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Before the Deep Umbra got changed into a stretch of the High Umbra in W20, there was, at most, one level, and it was because there was such a monumental quantity of self-loathing and fear of death in humans. If you want to call their disconnection and estrangement from the world around them special, that's great, but Werewolf doesn't tend to look on it favorably.</div> </div> </div> </div>The High Umbra is now a thing, but ignoring that there's still all sorts of spirits that are created as an offset of human action. Human endevours create more and different types of spirit than any other creature on the planet. And many of these spirits are found in broods of the wyld and gaia.<br /> <br /> Really, the fact that Garou might have a point but also be missing alot of the answers(and be fundimentally incapable of doing the job they were built for) is an important theme to the tragedy of the game, you can't just punch corruption in face until it gives up its more complicated than that.<br /> <br /> But this thread is also talking crossovers, to take a Technocratic view, the Garou are soldiers of an extradimensional entity that doesn't give a fuck about humanity at the very best and may potentially be hostile towards humanity and all its accomplishments. They don't care about good or evil they care about Corrupt and Pure. Corruption can be self driven but also external. When it comes down to it you have to ask what are the intrinsic worth of humans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T10:46:02-07:00","id":644410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=644161#post644161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The High Umbra is now a thing,</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't for the longest time. It doesn't fit well cramming in Mage's Umbra to Werewolf. Mage should never have touched the Umbra to begin with; they should have made a different otherworld to use just for Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but ignoring that there's still all sorts of spirits that are created as an offset of human action. Human endevours create more and different types of spirit than any other creature on the planet. And many of these spirits are found in broods of the wyld and gaia. </div> </div> </div>And that has more to do with coverage than inherent mystical importance. Of the latter, W:tA assumes, correctly, humans have none. Removing them isn't going to bring the system down. Like the Kings, they'll be gone eventually, and only the Mokole will remember them and care.<br /> <br /> Garou and Fera do have all the answers. They just find the tasks that are actually vital for success extremely difficult, and can be short-sighted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really, the fact that Garou might have a point but also be missing alot of the answers(and be fundimentally incapable of doing the job they were built for) is an important theme to the tragedy of the game, you can't just punch corruption in face until it gives up its more complicated than that.<br /> <br /> But this thread is also talking crossovers, to take a Technocratic view, the Garou are soldiers of an extradimensional entity that doesn't give a fuck about humanity at the very best and may potentially be hostile towards humanity and all its accomplishments. They don't care about good or evil they care about Corrupt and Pure. Corruption can be self driven but also external. When it comes down to it you have to ask what are the intrinsic worth of humans </div> </div> </div>Talking Mage is too big a break. Its greater cosmological assumptions are mutually exclusive to those of Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-29-2015, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T12:43:46-07:00","id":644525,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the settings were constructed as separate and unified at the same time.<br /> <br /> <b>Lian</b> is right, but not because it was intended. Werewolf would work perfectly under those assumptions, SOS, if it was a completely distinct setting. But it is only a partially distinct setting.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, doesn't mater if the Umbra wasn't supposed to be that way originally. That's how it is now. And, in setting, since always. Because the Werewolf perspective simply wasn't constructed with the current setting in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T13:54:20-07:00","id":644609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=644525#post644525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that the settings were constructed as separate and unified at the same time.<br /> <br /> <b>Lian</b> is right, but not because it was intended. Werewolf would work perfectly under those assumptions, SOS, if it was a completely distinct setting. But it is only a partially distinct setting.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, doesn't mater if the Umbra wasn't supposed to be that way originally. That's how it is now. And, in setting, since always. Because the Werewolf perspective simply wasn't constructed with the current setting in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>With V4's release, that's not such a certain thing, since if we get W4 it's likely going to follow off of Revised, which lacks that adjustment in W20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T14:24:02-07:00","id":644622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=644410#post644410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It wasn't for the longest time. It doesn't fit well cramming in Mage's Umbra to Werewolf. Mage should never have touched the Umbra to begin with; they should have made a different otherworld to use just for Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The HIGH umbra is special mage world Its always been that, since it was introduced in mage. We could call it Astral Realms like in NWod and ti wouldn't change a thing except CWod has some need to call the Underworld and Astral realms &quot;Umbras&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that has more to do with coverage than inherent mystical importance. Of the latter, W:tA assumes, correctly, humans have none. Removing them isn't going to bring the system down. Like the Kings, they'll be gone eventually, and only the Mokole will remember them and care. </div> </div> </div>If every human died tomorrow what would car spirits do? City Fathers? Computer spirits? Would they all be consumed by the wyrm and the orgy of epherma consumption be enough to pull the whole world down?<br /> <br /> Why were the Mokole the only changing breed for the Kings when Humanity has Countless Variations? Why were the Garou promoted now to Fight the Wyrm and not some sort of wereraptor before the Wonder work? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Garou and Fera do have all the answers. They just find the tasks that are actually vital for success extremely difficult, and can be short-sighted. </div> </div> </div>IF they have all the answers then why do they disagree about fundimental aspects of reality? Hell the Zhong Lung don't even believe in Kings.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Talking Mage is too big a break. Its greater cosmological assumptions are mutually exclusive to those of Werewolf. </div> </div> </div>Talking vampire is too big a break. Its greater cosmological assumptions are mutually exclusive to those of werewolf too. We started with the morality of the Camarilla vs the Garou Nation. Which is intrinsically a question of crossover and I am not even talking the whole subjective reality I'm saying from the perspective of Human first technology is awesome group the Garou are warriors of an Alien monster that has little regard for humanity. You said so yourself the perspective of garou is humans have no mystic importance. And perhaps in Werewolf this is true, but when we start talking crossover(and once you mention vampires as anything more than Wyrm servants its crossover) the Fera lose that potential rightness. You can ask the question &quot;Is nature more important than people&quot; and when you say deep down no, that the reason we protect the world is for people not the other way around the Fera lose theri Paladin status and become another set of scary monsters.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T02:04:43-07:00","id":645185,"title":"","content":"Ahem. You are both ignoring one key fact, though. Werewolves are humans. And even if their religion and their allies tell them that humans do not matter, Werewolves will care for humans, because at the end even most lupus will feel a kinship for them. They are their lovers, their fathers, their daughter, their drinking buddies and the fathers of their children. They tried to do &quot;what should be done&quot; thousands of years ago... they realised they were wrong and couldn't do that to their own. That choice clearly shows that the Garou do care for humanity. If they didn't, they could have sorted it out with Rorg to deal with it aeons ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T04:23:30-07:00","id":645275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=644609#post644609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With V4's release, that's not such a certain thing, since if we get W4 it's likely going to follow off of Revised, which lacks that adjustment in W20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the adjustment won't change a thing, because what renders the Fera's reasoning wrong is the crossover itself.<br /> <br /> If you work Werewolf as standalone, you're right. If you run it as just a part of the cWoD setting, you're wrong, and it is as simple as that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T04:36:19-07:00","id":645282,"title":"","content":"Actually there is one cWoD for each of the splats, you know. It has Mages, Technocracies, Changelings, Vampires and shit. It's just that they are backup cast and don't really matter as much. So he's not really doing it wrong. A proper joint cWoD doesn't really exist. All the attempts at crossover books were widely panned and never really tried to actually sort out what a &quot;join&quot; cWoD would actually be like. So any joint cWoD we discuss is wholly a creation of the fanbase.<br /> <br /> ... and that, kids, is why we still argue like grumpy old men.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 08-30-2015, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T06:55:48-07:00","id":645369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=645185#post645185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahem. You are both ignoring one key fact, though. Werewolves are humans. And even if their religion and their allies tell them that humans do not matter, Werewolves will care for humans, because at the end even most lupus will feel a kinship for them. They are their lovers, their fathers, their daughter, their drinking buddies and the fathers of their children. They tried to do &quot;what should be done&quot; thousands of years ago... they realised they were wrong and couldn't do that to their own. That choice clearly shows that the Garou do care for humanity. If they didn't, they could have sorted it out with Rorg to deal with it aeons ago.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, Fera aren't human. I mean they have a human shape but their instincts and spirit qualities as much separate them from Humanity as their sapience separates them from their beastkin. A sizeable minority thinks giving up the culling was a mistake. A larger faction would be more than happy to kick humanity back down to what they consider &quot;the glory days&quot; if they could only really the Glasswalkers and Bonegnawers have any buy for modern civilization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T09:56:27-07:00","id":645540,"title":"","content":"You're mixing up the partyline and who they really are. Most of them are born human and most of them have human families, heck Lupus born breed with humans at times. For all intents and purposes they are as much man as they are spirit and wolf, and that's something that needs to be taken into account, especially since it seems that the man part may be the one that's the loudest. Just take a look at the tribebooks and all the in character stuff. They care quite a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T19:13:45-07:00","id":646196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=645540#post645540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're mixing up the partyline and who they really are. Most of them are born human and most of them have human families, heck Lupus born breed with humans at times. For all intents and purposes they are as much man as they are spirit and wolf, and that's something that needs to be taken into account, especially since it seems that the man part may be the one that's the loudest. Just take a look at the tribebooks and all the in character stuff. They care quite a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most people don't care about most people, monkey sphere and all. Most Fera don't give a crap about humans outside their sphere, and most seem to actively hate the modern world. So a solar flare that caused a society colapse and pushed things back to preindustrial times would be I think up their alley.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T07:19:57-07:00","id":661863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=644161#post644161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But this thread is also talking crossovers, to take a Technocratic view, the Garou are soldiers of an extradimensional entity that doesn't give a fuck about humanity at the very best and may potentially be hostile towards humanity and all its accomplishments. They don't care about good or evil they care about Corrupt and Pure. Corruption can be self driven but also external. When it comes down to it you have to ask what are the intrinsic worth of humans</div> </div> </div> </div>From a Techno view, garou are basically like the Chthulu cults in Lovecraft's old stories. They are grotesquely alien in body, mind, and soul, and they worship utterly alien horrors from beyond.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T23:45:36-07:00","id":662732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/637473-question-regarding-working-together-and-good-vs-evil?p=661863#post661863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From a Techno view, garou are basically like the Chthulu cults in Lovecraft's old stories. They are grotesquely alien in body, mind, and soul, and they worship utterly alien horrors from beyond.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well they are more full on Deep One hybrids, creatures of alien nature and unnatural lineage serving uncaring monsters. Now Garou should be the heroes of theirown stories, but when you use them as npcs its worth considering presenting them less as Chosen Holy Warriors of the Earth Mother but rather more sinister options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T09:14:37-07:00","id":663219,"title":"","content":"Typically, a werewolf's enemies don't see the faith. They just see the teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}